7-Eleven confirmed a breach of systems storing franchisee documents affecting about 50 people in three US state filings; the 600,000+ Salesforce records are ShinyHunters' unverified claim, which 7-Eleven has not addressed. SecurityWeek describes ShinyHunters' Salesforce intrusions in general as phishing, third-party-integration abuse or misconfigurations and lists Instructure, Vimeo, Wynn Resorts, Vercel and Medtronic as other recent claims, without tying them or a vector to the 7-Eleven breach. CyberInsider links Charter's listing to the Salesforce-focused campaign but gives no access vector for it.
